  File "tests/rejected/while_no_measure.py", line 7
    while i < n:
TypeCheckError: the checker has to see that a while loop ends. It sees it by itself for 'while i < n:' where the last statement is 'i += 1' (i a Nat, n not changed in the loop), and for 'while k > 0:' where the last statement is 'k -= 1' (k an int). Any other while loop ends with decreases(measure, proof): the measure is a Nat worked out from the loop's variables, and the proof shows (new measure < old measure) == True. A for loop needs none of this.
